//? Title: FCOS anchor-free points, centerness and IoU fitting
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Verify tensor point assignment and every derivative of focal, centerness and IoU objectives, check the full FCOS graph, then explicitly fit the complete compact detector with paired BN checkpoints and real digit-scene galleries.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/fcos.cpp`.

> The method

FCOS replaces anchor shapes with per-point l/t/r/b distances and centerness. Shared group-normalized towers operate over P3–P7, while eligibility ranges and smallest-area matching assign tensor targets.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/fcos_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/fcos_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/fcos_concept.tikz > build/fcos_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/fcos_concept.svg build/fcos_concept.dvi > build/fcos_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
