> Full graph and compact source adaptation

Full FCOS has 36,426,138 learned and 53,120 BN-state scalars, a ResNet50
backbone, 256-channel FPN and shared four-layer GN32 towers. Centerness comes
from the **classification** tower, following the original source model. Each
pyramid level learns a scalar before `exp(min(raw*scale,20))`; distances are
positive. The full source graph below checks all 218 learned tensor derivatives
at 128 pixels, and counts 8525 predictions at 640. It is initialized validation,
without pretraining or a trained COCO claim.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
  n::models::FcosConfig c;
  c.image_size = 128;
  c.update_stats = false;
  const auto net = n::models::Fcos(
      p, state, n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 128 * 128 * 3)).reshape({1, 128, 128, 3}), c, true);
  if (p.count() != 36426138 || state.count() != 53120 || net.points != 341)
    return 1;
  const auto objective = n::mean(n::square(net.logits)) + n::mean(n::square(net.distances)) +
                         n::mean(n::square(net.centerness));
  const auto g = n::grad(objective, p.parameters());
  if (g.size() != 218)
    return 1;
  for (const auto &v : g)
    if (!v.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(v)).item()))
      return 1;
  std::print("Full-weight FCOS128: {} learned/{} state scalars,{} points; all{} learned "
             "tensor derivatives defined and finite. Full640: {} points.\n",
             p.count(), state.count(), net.points, g.size(),
             n::models::FcosPoints({80, 40, 20, 10, 5}).shape()[0]);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Full-weight FCOS128: 36426138 learned/53120 state scalars,341 points; all218 learned tensor derivatives defined and finite. Full640: 8525 points.
// result_end

The compact source adaptation uses ResNet18 with widths divided by eight,
32-channel FPN/GN8 towers, 314,684 learned and 1,200 BN-state scalars. This
report uses 64-pixel scenes, range multiplier .125 and stride-scaled exp
distances (the source's larger128-pixel run uses range multiplier .25).
Every backbone/tower/scale parameter is fitted. The split is the same bounded
64 fit/16 validation and eight test MNIST-derived scenes used by the other
detection reports. No test scene selects epochs.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fcos_scenes.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto train = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "train");
  n::models::DetectionSceneConfig cfg;
  cfg.scenes = 80;
  cfg.seed = 11;
  const auto scenes = n::models::MakeTensorDetectionScenes(
      n::slice_axis(train.images, 0, 0, 2048), n::slice_axis(train.labels, 0, 0, 2048), cfg);

  std::vector<n::Tensor> boxes(scenes.boxes.begin(), scenes.boxes.begin() + 8);
  const auto preview = n::models::DrawDetectionBoxes(n::slice_axis(scenes.images, 0, 0, 8),
                                                     boxes, {.1, 1., .2});
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(preview, "build/fcos_scenes.png", 4, 0., 1., 4, 1., 2);
  std::int64_t objects = 0;
  for (const auto &b : scenes.boxes)
    objects += b.shape()[0];
  std::print("80 generated training/validation scenes; {} accepted digits. Preview: first "
             "eight training scenes with tight green boxes.\n",
             objects);
}
