\caption(Explicit whole-network FCOS Adam fitting, with focal and combined centre/IoU terms, validation AP50 and backbone moving-state history. Both checkpoint stores are restored before held-out evaluation.)
\alttext(Explicit whole-network FCOS Adam fitting, with focal and combined centre/IoU terms, validation AP50 and backbone moving-state history. Both checkpoint stores are restored before held-out evaluation.)

\image(figures/fcos_detections.png)
\caption(Actual held-out compact FCOS detections in red and ground truth in green. Mislocalization, extra detections and class errors remain part of the measured result.)
\alttext(Eight held-out digit scenes with true and predicted FCOS boxes.)

> Conclusion

The selected epoch15 has validation AP50 .043993. Test AP50/AP75/AP50:95 are .018984/.003507/.005745, with the 100/image cap reached in all eight scenes. Decreasing training loss has not produced a useful held-out detector in this bounded schedule; the report preserves the visible false positives.

Point/range semantics and the complete objective are checked before fitting. The bounded compact run evaluates its restored validation-selected parameters and BN state on held-out scenes; it does not claim full-dataset detector accuracy.

> References

- [Tian et al. (2019), FCOS: Fully Convolutional One-Stage Object Detection](https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.01355).
- [Authors’ FCOS implementation](https://github.com/tianzhi0549/FCOS).
